Measurement harness for the multipath filter's startup wait
(doc/MULTIPATH_WAITING_20260812.md and doc/MULTIPATH_QMM_20260813.md).

Apply to a throwaway `git worktree` checkout, never to the main tree:

    git worktree add --detach /tmp/mfwait dev
    cp -R r8brain-free-src /tmp/mfwait/ && rm -f /tmp/mfwait/r8brain-free-src/.git
    git -C /tmp/mfwait apply /path/to/this.diff
    cmake -S /tmp/mfwait -B /tmp/mfwait/build-dbg \
      -DEXTRA_FLAGS="-DCOEFF_MONITOR=1 -DDEBUG_MULTIPATH_FILTER=1 \
                     -DDEBUG_MF_RESET=1 -DDEBUG_MF_ERR=1 -DDEBUG_AGC_TRACE=1"
    cmake --build /tmp/mfwait/build-dbg --target airspy-fmradion -j

It adds two things to sfmbase/FmDecode.cpp, both inert in a normal build:

1. m_wait_multipath_blocks is read once from the MF_WAIT_BLOCKS environment
   variable (default 20, the shipped value), so one binary covers every wait
   under test instead of one build per value.  The value actually used is
   echoed to stderr as `MFWAIT,<n>` so each run's log records its own setting.
   This costs one function-local static read at construction and is otherwise
   identical to the compiled-in constant; it was verified bit-exact against a
   compile-time macro build before use.

2. Three stderr-only, #ifdef-guarded traces, following the existing
   COEFF_MONITOR / DEBUG_PLL_FILTER convention of doc/MF_DEBUG_CODE_20260726.md.
   All default off; no DSP arithmetic is touched.

     DEBUG_AGC_TRACE  AGCTRACE,<block>,<IF AGC gain>,<waiting?>   every block
     DEBUG_MF_ERR     MFERR,<block>,<peak |output|>,<CMA error>   filtered blocks
     DEBUG_MF_RESET   MFRESET,<block>                             divergence resets

   <block> is the true FmDecoder::process() call index in all three, so traces
   from runs with different wait lengths line up sample for sample.

Verified 2026-08-13 against dev at 48f162c: applies cleanly, builds with the
flags above, and MFERR first appears at exactly block <wait>.

